# GEOSIX frontend environment variables
#
# This is a template, not a configuration file. Copy it and edit the copy:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FOR `npm run dev` ONLY. NOTHING HERE IS USED BY THE DOCKER IMAGE.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `VITE_API_BASE_URL` is a BUILD-TIME variable: Vite inlines it into the compiled
# JavaScript bundle, so whatever it is set to becomes part of the shipped asset.
#
# Leave it empty (the shipped default) so api-client.ts uses the relative base ""
# and the browser calls `/api/v1/...` on its own origin. The Vite dev server proxies
# /api to http://localhost:8000 (see vite.config.ts), which is what makes that work
# without any CORS preflight.
#
# The containerized frontend works the same way, one level up: frontend/nginx
# proxies /api/ to the backend service. That is why frontend/Dockerfile
# deliberately does NOT set or ARG this variable -- baking a backend hostname into
# the image would tie it to a single environment and would make the browser depend
# on a Compose-internal hostname that does not resolve outside the Compose network.
#
# See docs/deployment.md for the deployment architecture.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=